Z||000000||Philphine||07-13-2000||09:59 AM||||<BR>anyone felt the need to leave neg. feedback on ebay. what were the circumstances and how long did you wait to do it. my latest purchase is going very badly and i'm thinking neg. feed back will only make it worse or kill it all together.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-13-2000||10:11 AM||||I have left negative feedback on both Ebay and Yahoo. On Ebay I sold an Item and never got a reply back from the buyer. I waited a week and sent many Emails. Finally after I sent the negative feedback they sent me a very abusive Email. Ebay was sent a copy and kicked the people off. On yahoo I have had to send negative feedback more often. More people bid and no one buys.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||07-13-2000||02:02 PM||||I only left neg. feedback on ebay once.  It was a dutch auction and like 5 other people bid on it.  I emailed the guy a bunch of times and nothing.  Then he emails me and says he has decided not to sell it.  Come to find out, he sent his address to a couple of the other people and they sent him money and got nothing.  I guess I was lucky...||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||07-13-2000||06:55 PM||||i never had a problem with anyone on ebay yet, i usually buy car stuff, tools, and some collectible items.<P>If i was buying something from someone.  I would wait until i got the item then leave a negative feedback.  Ebay suggests 3 days maxiumum of communication between buyer and seller after the bid.<P>I usually email the person saying heres my address and how much is the total, and telling them how long its gonna take me to send my moneyorder.  They reply back with their info.  I send the moneyorder, and usually inform them that i did.  Some sellers reply back that they got it and they are sending the item.   <BR>The longest i had to wait for an item was less then 10 days.<P>You dont want to piss off anyone, because they can keep your money.  There are people who can switch info and get a different account on ebay.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||07-14-2000||11:08 AM||||thats one good thing, i haven't sent any money. i just can't get them to finish the deal and now haven't heard from them for 2 weeks. the auction ended over 3 weeks ago. i'm dealing with two companies that have joined to sell something but they seem compleatly unorganized on that end. one side is friendly and i have contacted them a few times, but the other group is handling the actual sale.<P>when i call to speak to the person i've been told to contact he's never in. i admit one problem is that i'm on es time and they are west coast, plus i work 2nd shift and can't call at work. after about 3-5 days of calling and them not knowing what i was talking about they got very rude and said i shouldn't even have that phone number.<P>i finaly went back to the first group (it actualy took me a while to realise i was dealing with 2 groups) they said they'd take care of it, but now i haven't heard from them either. the bad thing is it's a set of wheels i really want and could never afford new (about $3000, 18" antera 109's) so i want the deal to go through. but after so much time i guess i'm holding out hope for nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||07-14-2000||03:14 PM||||<BR>The thing is, even if you re-establish contact with these people, do you really want to send them money after all this hassle. Then what would happen? I think you should consider yourself lucky that all you've lost up to this point is time. I say submit the negative feedback and then be done with it. ||||reg||13
